---CloneJob describes the process of creating a clone of a MigratingVM to the requested target based on the latest successful uploaded snapshots. While the migration cycles of a MigratingVm take place, it is possible to verify the uploaded VM can be started in the cloud, by creating a clone. The clone can be created without any downtime, and it is created using the latest snapshots which are already in the cloud. The cloneJob is only responsible for its work, not its products, which means once it is finished, it will never touch the instance it created. It will only delete it in case of the CloneJob being cancelled or upon failure to clone.
---@class gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.CloneJob
---@field computeEngineDisksTargetDetails? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.ComputeEngineDisksTargetDetails Output only. Details of the target Persistent Disks in Compute Engine.
---@field state? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.CloneJobStateEnum|string Output only. State of the clone job.
---@field stateTime? string Output only. The time the state was last updated.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the clone job was ended.
---@field steps? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.CloneStepList Output only. The clone steps list representing its progress.
---@field targetDetails? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.TargetVMDetails Output only. Details of the VM to create as the target of this clone job. Deprecated: Use compute_engine_target_details instead.
---@field computeEngineTargetDetails? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.ComputeEngineTargetDetails Output only. Details of the target VM in Compute Engine.
---@field name? string Output only. The name of the clone.
---@field computeEngineVmDetails? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.TargetVMDetails Output only. Details of the VM in Compute Engine. Deprecated: Use compute_engine_target_details instead.
---@field error? gcp.unstable.vmmigration_v1alpha1.Status Output only. Provides details for the errors that led to the Clone Job's state.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the clone job was created (as an API call, not when it was actually created in the target).

